  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d4aec768",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: when_you_chop_onions; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person making a face of discomfort or distress, with hands framing their eyes, while the text \"when you chop onions\" is overlaid. This is a common meme used to humorously convey the physical discomfort caused by chopping onions, which releases sulfur compounds that irritate the eyes. The scene is not inherently toxic or harmful in a discriminatory sense. However, the meme's intent is to evoke a relatable, mildly unpleasant experience through exaggerated facial expression. While not abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, or propagandistic, it could be considered \"harmful\" in a very mild, non-malicious way if interpreted as mocking someone's sensitivity or inability to handle a basic kitchen task. The meme relies on the universal experience of onion-induced tears, and there is no targeting of any protected group or harmful stereotype. The intent is purely to create a humorous, relatable analogy: the visual of the person's pained expression is mapped onto the textual description of the mundane, irritating task of chopping onions, aiming to elicit laughter or empathy from viewers who have experienced the same.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_79da4a7c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
